  "reason": "The name 'full retraining of a language model' refers to the specific process of recalculating all internal parameters. The existing concept 'language model retraining' is defined as the process of updating a language model's internal parameters using new data. While related, they are not identical in scope: 'full retraining' implies a complete recalculation of the entire parameter set (often from scratch or full fine-tuning), whereas 'retraining' can broadly include partial updates or fine-tuning subsets. The definitions distinguish between the completeness of the process ('all internal parameters' vs 'updating... using new data'). Therefore, substituting one for the other alters the specific referent regarding the extent of parameter modification.",
  "distinction": "Scope difference: 'full retraining' specifies recalculating all parameters, while 'language model retraining' allows for general updates which may not be full.",
